# WGSL

## Registration

- Import new sources in `src/shaders/registry.js` with `?raw`.
- Shared libs → `ShaderStore.IncludesShadersStoreWGSL` under `snow*` keys; pull in with `#include<snowFoo>`.
- Full stages → `ShaderStore.ShadersStoreWGSL` as `<name>VertexShader` / `<name>PixelShader` (Babylon WGSL naming).
- Call `registerShaders()` once before any material is built (done in `main.js`).

## Shared includes (`lib/`)

| Include | Role |
|---------|------|
| `snowNoise` / `snowTerrain` | height / landform (bake + runtime must stay identical) |
| `snowDeform` | deformation buffer sample / displace |
| `snowShading` | BRDF, SSS, glints, shadow filter |
| `snowShadowLookup` | cascade PCSS |
| `snowAtmosphere` | fog / aerial / sky LUT lookups |
| `snowClipmap` | clipmap vertex placement |
| `snowCharSkin` / `snowWake` / `snowWater` / `snowCrystal` | domain geometry |
| `snowSpellLights` | four-slot dynamic light pool |
| `snowPostCommon` | post helpers |

Bake passes and beauty passes that share landform logic must `#include` the same lib text — do not duplicate formulas in JS or a second WGSL copy.

## Conventions

- Prefer explanatory header comments for non-obvious math (order of normal combination, sign of light vectors, etc.).
- Match existing uniform/texture naming on sibling materials so CPU upload paths stay consistent.
- Depth / prepass variants reuse the beauty vertex placement includes where possible; only diverge for discard/alpha cases (e.g. wake prepass).
